WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.883
Most people picture a battery inside a phone or car

00:00:03.883 --> 00:00:07.080
This one is built for the electricity grid

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:16.444
Form Energy is developing and commercialising iron-air storage designed to deliver electricity for up to one hundred hours.

00:00:16.444 --> 00:00:18.660
The company is Form Energy

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:25.904
Its Form Factory One is in Weirton, West Virginia, on the site of a former steel mill

00:00:25.904 --> 00:00:29.909
These diagrams explain its published technology

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:35.363
They are illustrations, not footage of its factory or equipment.

00:00:35.363 --> 00:00:42.950
During discharge, iron reacts with oxygen and becomes rust, releasing stored electrical energy

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:47.227
Charging reverses that reaction and restores the iron

00:00:47.227 --> 00:00:53.038
The system stores energy supplied to it; it does not create free energy.

00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:59.834
Form describes cells containing iron and air electrodes with a water-based electrolyte

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:05.603
Cells are assembled into modules, then grouped into protective enclosures

00:01:05.603 --> 00:01:11.847
This is the public system architecture, not a proprietary manufacturing recipe.

00:01:11.847 --> 00:01:18.363
The company describes electrode production and cell assembly lines at its factory

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:24.718
Its published equipment needs include coating, pressing, welding and automation

00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:32.039
Exact materials, settings, quality limits and assembly instructions are not disclosed here.

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:39.068
Form reports grid-connected test systems in California and commercial agreements with utilities

00:01:39.068 --> 00:01:46.097
Testing a system and signing an agreement are different from operating a large commercial fleet

00:01:46.097 --> 00:01:50.832
The technology is moving from pilots into commercial deployment.

00:01:50.832 --> 00:01:59.970
Multi-day storage is intended to help electricity grids through extended shortages and periods of low renewable output

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:07.946
Duration alone is not enough: operators also need reliable performance, suitable sites and viable costs

00:02:07.946 --> 00:02:13.290
Read the linked manufacturer sources for the evidence and its limits.
